course: dictionary
lesson: 16067
title: Words that show choice
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Voluntarily is an adverb. It tells you how someone did something: they did it by choice. «Mia voluntarily helped clean the park.» Nobody told her to, and she was not forced.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Did someone have to do it? If not, the action was voluntary. «Sam was not asked to go; he joined the charity walk voluntarily.» The words «not asked» are the clue. Check your meaning by swapping it in: «Sam joined the walk by choice» still makes sense, so voluntarily means by choice.
explain: The formal version is «of your own free will». «He voluntarily handed himself in to the police» tells us he chose to go, and nobody forced him. Voluntary is the adjective, so a voluntary job is one you do by choice, often without pay.
fact: Voluntarily means by choice, without being forced.
fact: Voluntarily is an adverb: it tells you how an action was done.
fact: Voluntarily can also mean without being paid, as with volunteers at charity events.
fact: «Of your own free will» is a formal phrase that means the same as voluntarily.
fact: The opposite of voluntarily is being forced or made to do something.
exercise: «Mia voluntarily helped clean the park on Saturday.» What does voluntarily mean? | Because her teacher told her to | Very quickly and loudly | Angrily, after an argument | *Because she chose to, not because she was forced
exercise: «Sam was not asked to go; he joined the walk voluntarily.» Which clue shows that Sam chose to go? | *not asked | Sam | walk | joined
exercise: Which phrase means the same as voluntarily? | Under orders | By accident | *Of your own free will | Very carefully
test: «The students cleaned the beach voluntarily on Sunday.» Why did they do it? | Because they were paid a lot | Because the head teacher made them | Because it was raining | *Because they chose to
test: Which sentence shows someone acting voluntarily? | Ravi was taken to the office by a guard | *Ravi offered to help carry the bags, and nobody asked him | Ravi was told to sweep the floor by his mum | Ravi was sent to his room for talking
exam: Read «She voluntarily gave up her lunch break to tidy the library.» What does voluntarily tell you about her? | *She chose to do it, of her own free will | She was paid extra to do it | She did it by accident | She was made to do it by the librarian
